! Baseline + crowding (AA3)

In the published model each plot belongs to one household (Janssen 2009, section 2.14). Here, when no empty plot is available anywhere, a relocating or newly formed household may join an occupied plot, up to `crowding-limit` households, if its share of the plot's output still meets the 800 kg nutrition need. Households therefore accept crowding only as land runs out. With `crowding-limit` = 1 the model matches the [[Baseline]].

